  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9c7c506b-d743-5338-9588-9b247598c315" activityNameId="a1131274-04cf-54a6-9f9a-5c854edb3915" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Lithium carbonate, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Lithium carbonate, at plant
The dataset can be used for preparing electrode base material for batteries. Data are based on an environmental survey from SEIA-CONAMA (2006). Infrastructure: ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are calculated in detail, based on the environmental survey.The plant uses liquified gas. Liquified gas is not available as "heat…" or "burned…" .  Thus we balanced more "natural gas, burned..." and made a credit for preparation of "natural gas, high pressure". ;
CAS number: 000554-13-2; 
Formula: Li2CO3; 
Synonyms: Li2CO3; 
UUID: 2f4a8d1a-d27a-39c5-9370-8a2776ec7326
Concentrated lithium brine is treated with additives for the removal of boron, followed by a purification step. Finally, the addition of soda for carbonation results in the precipitation of lithium carbonate (Li2CO3). The salt is filtered, washed and dried and subsequently reaches a purity of 99.2%
Location: Production site is in Chile, all data originate from an environmental survey about the plant in Chile. This dataset can be used globally, as this plant produces 70% of the Li2CO3 worldwide.
Technology: The concentrated lithium brine is treated with additives for the removal of boron, followed by a purification step.  Finally, the addition of soda for carbonation results in the precipitation of lithium carbonate (Li2CO3).
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: ecoinvental survey 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2f4a8d1a-d27a-39c5-9370-8a2776ec7326.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
